.TH LOCALPASSKEY 1 "October 2026" "localpasskey 0.1.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
localpasskey \- list and delete the passkeys stored on this computer
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B localpasskey list
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.RB [ \-\-user
.IR user ]
.br
.B localpasskey delete
.RI [ ID ...]
.RB [ \-\-site
.IR site ]
.RB [ \-\-all ]
.RB [ \-\-user
.IR user ]
.RB [ \-y ]
.br
.B localpasskey status
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B localpasskey
talks to
.BR localpasskeyd (8),
which keeps passkeys for websites on this computer. Every user only sees
and manages their own passkeys; root can act on any user's with
.BR \-\-user .
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B list
Show your passkeys: an ID, the site, the account, whether it is a
.I passkey
(usable without typing a user name) or a
.I security key
(a second factor the site asks for by ID), and when it was created and last
used.
.B \-\-json
prints all details.
.TP
.B delete
Delete the passkeys given by
.I ID
(or any unique prefix of at least four characters), all passkeys for
.BR \-\-site ,
or
.B \-\-all
of them. The command shows what will be deleted and asks for
confirmation (skip with
.BR \-y ),
then polkit asks for your password. Deleting a passkey here does not remove
it from the website's account settings.
.TP
.B status
Check that the service is running and show the virtual device node.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
$ localpasskey list
ID            SITE        ACCOUNT                    TYPE     CREATED           LAST USED
3f9a1c2d55e0  github.com  octocat                    passkey  2026-10-08 06:31  2026-10-08 06:40
$ localpasskey delete 3f9a
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR localpasskeyd (8)
